id: pm-gh1695
title: "GH-1695: accept settings paths and provide bounded config-key recovery"
description: "Canonical intake for https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1695. Implement the reported SDK and CLI recovery contract after current-source reproduction, preserving deterministic validation, privacy and no-write refusal behavior."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[4]: agent-ux,config,"gh:1695",sdk
created_at: "2026-11-09T07:32:05.563Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-09T10:27:55.690Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-09T10:27:54.354Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-09T10:27:54.354Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Accept every supported settings path as an alias in SDK-backed config get/set without bypassing validation; Unknown keys offer at most three nearest legal keys and a working config-list inspection command; Preserve complete legal keys in structured recovery and reject unknown keys without settings writes
parent: pm-8jdc
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Supported settings paths reuse canonical SDK validation and scope; context leaves round-trip through the shared read/write depth domain including full. Unknown-key recovery is bounded, scope-aware and deterministic for both equal- and unequal-distance candidate sets."
expected_result: "Dotted/canonical keys share validated persistence and scope, and multi-candidate recovery orders by distance then canonical key without writes on invalid input."
actual_result: The full-depth SDK round-trip failed before the settings validator fix and passes afterward. The 171-test settings/guidance/parser cohort and final 168-test instrumented owner cohort pass; changed config suggestion/leaf and human-domain branches have no uncovered markers. Focused instrumentation intentionally fails whole-source thresholds outside its selected files; required complete CI coverage remains unwaived. Linked configuration tests pass again.
